cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this model or its outputs, please cite it as below. The numbers
  of a release are those of its full run (python run_all.py), committed under
  outputs/ and locked by tests/test_regression_model_v1.py and
  tests/test_regression_model_v2.py.
type: software
title: >-
  New Zealand new residential floor area and embodied carbon, 2026–2050:
  projection, planetary-boundary layer (AESA) and pathways
version: 2.1.0
authors:
  - family-names: Christoforatos
    given-names: Gerasimos
repository-code: "https://github.com/GerasimosChristoforatos/Pathway-Paper"
abstract: >-
  A bottom-up, demand-driven projection of the new residential floor area New
  Zealand builds in 2026–2050 and its embodied carbon (materials and
  construction A1–A5, soil carbon loss, maintenance B2/B4, and the emissions
  committed after 2050), with Monte Carlo and Sobol uncertainty analysis,
  validation against the census record, an absolute environmental
  sustainability assessment (AESA) of climate change under the acquired-rights
  and ability-to-pay allocation principles, and five construction pathways
  built from five levers with Shapley attribution, a back-cast, a
  hyper-optimistic theoretical limit and a pathway Monte Carlo of the
  Reference, the combined pathway and the theoretical limit.
keywords:
  - embodied carbon
  - residential construction
  - floor area projection
  - absolute environmental sustainability assessment
  - planetary boundaries
  - New Zealand
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Embodied impacts of residential stocks; multi-level assessment of
      materials, buildings, typologies and functional units to support
      policymaking towards sustainable housing
